            <div xml:id="d498">

                <pb facs="0659" n="563" xml:id="pg563"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/2829: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-11-26T17:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 26,
                                1921—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 27—7
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>127. Department’s telegram 43, November 22, 1 p.m. There will be no difficulty
                    regarding passage over Honduranean territory of officer and escort provided they
                    do not have character of an armed force. According to Honduranean Constitution
                    authority to permit entry of armed force lies with Congress. President therefore
                    suggests that escort carry only side arms. The President wishes to extend every
                    facility to the party and requests that he be informed of date and place arrival
                    at frontier.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
